+**Relationship and savings.** Act 8 controls Founder priorities, quality,
+timeliness, attention economy, and later expressed Founder preferences; this
+proposal supplies only a defeasible operational choice rule subordinate to
+those priorities and reserved authority. Act 15 preserves Judiciary
+independence: the Judiciary may investigate, measure, and report, but does not
+own implementation of its recommendations. Act 21 remains the complete
+authority for its exact-commit/tree, applicable-suite, merge-verification,
+durable record, and audit requirements; none are restated, replaced, or
+relaxed here. Act 23 remains controlling for office responsibilities,
+independent closure, durable evidence, and continuity; this proposal is a
+narrow coordination clarification and adds no independent closure substitute.
+In any conflict, these Acts and the Constitution control.
